  "aiContextParagraph": "The death of veteran Nigerian actor Pete Edochie, 79, has prompted a wave of national mourning. Reports confirm that the actor passed away in Enugu after battling prostate cancer. Widely regarded as a foundational figure in the Nollywood film industry, Edochie gained significant recognition for his role as Okonkwo in the adaptation of Things Fall Apart. Tributes have poured in from political leadership, including President Bola Tinubu, who lauded the late actor's role in promoting Nigerian cultural identity globally. Additionally, Enugu State Governor Peter Mbah expressed deep condolences, describing the loss as a major impact on both the state and the nation. Fellow actors and family members, including May Edochie, have remembered him as a legendary institution within the arts, acknowledging his long-standing influence on the craft of acting and his status as a national icon.",
